# Semi-Supervised Learning on MNIST

Comparing semi-supervised learning approaches on MNIST digit classification,
using a small labelled set and large unlabelled pool.

## Key Result
Self-training with MLP achieved 7.5% pseudo-label error rate,
significantly outperforming Label Propagation (89.7% error) on 
high-dimensional pixel data.

## Methods Compared
- Self-training with MLP classifier
- Label Propagation

## Key Finding
Label Propagation degrades on high-dimensional data (784 pixel features)
because distance metrics become unreliable in high dimensions.
Self-training with a strong base classifier handles this effectively.

## Tech
Python, scikit-learn, NumPy, Matplotlib
